  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nWhat is the applicable date for filing the individual annual income tax return in the Philippines?\n\n### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing the individual annual income tax return is April 15 of the following year after the taxable year.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nTaxpayers should prepare their income tax returns in advance of the April 15 deadline to avoid penalties for late filing. It is advisable to gather all necessary documentation, such as income statements and deductions, well before this date to ensure a smooth filing process. Additionally, taxpayers should be aware of any changes in tax laws or regulations that may affect their filing requirements for the current tax year.",
